Subject: Upstream Wine fixes needed to cross-build the PE side with llvm-mingw (adapted to the CrossOver 26.3 tree)
Origin: Gcenx/macports-wine, emulators/wine-stable/files/llvm-mingw_fixes.patch — nine cherry-picks from upstream Wine:
        ntdll syscall dispatch split into unix/syscall.c; ARM64 KiUserExceptionDispatcher machine frame;
        macOS ARM64 stack-packing ABI wrapper; winegcc --cc-cmd; winebuild locating llvm-* tools;
        makedep passing CC through; two test fixes.
Changed-by: SSF Play — adapted by hand to crossover-sources-26.3.0 (sources/wine). One hunk in
        dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c conflicts with CodeWeavers' "CW Hack 24067", so the original file cannot be applied as is.
Date-of-change: 2026-07-30
Files: tools/winegcc/winegcc.c, tools/winebuild/*, tools/makedep.c, dlls/ntdll/unix/* and others (see the diff below)
Effect: Wine 11.0 builds with llvm-mingw for x86_64 + i386. The ARM64 parts compile but are not used by this x86_64 build.
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine.
